## 1. Executive Problem Statement

Blanket promotional discounting often erodes retail profit margins without increasing long-term customer lifetime value (LTV) or average order value (AOV). This project analyzes **3,900 retail transactions** across **50 US states** using Python, MS SQL Server (`dbo.customer_behavior`), and Power BI to evaluate demographic buying patterns, subscription tier performance, and product discount dependency, translating those insights into a **Tiered Loyalty & Minimum-Spend Promo Engine BRD**.

- **Analytical Baseline:** Modeled **3,900 customer orders** (mean spend **$59.76 USD**, overall median **$60.00 USD**, mean rating **3.75/5.0**). Found that **43.0% of all transactions (1,677 orders)** used a discount/promo code, while **73.0% of shoppers (2,847 customers)** remain unsubscribed (`subscription_status = 'No'`) despite an average history of **25.35 previous purchases**.
- **What-If Opportunity Sizing (Dataset Simulation):** Historical transaction analysis reveals that **50%** of all discounted orders (`discount_applied = 'Yes'`) fell below the discounted cohort's median basket size of **$60 USD**, eroding margins on small checkouts. Simulating a **Minimum-Spend Promo Threshold** (requiring a **$60+ USD** cart to unlock promo codes) shows that if just **25%** of sub-median discount shoppers add items to meet the threshold, the store captures **$4452.75 USD in incremental revenue** (a **4.5%** lift across the discounted cohort).

<details>
<summary><b>🔍 View SQL Logic Used for Opportunity Sizing (from 02_business_analysis.sql)</b></summary>

```sql
WITH order_stats AS (
    SELECT purchase_amount,
           discount_applied,
           PERCENTILE_CONT(0.5) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY purchase_amount) OVER () AS median_aov
    FROM customer_behavior
    WHERE discount_applied = 'Yes'
)
SELECT MAX(median_aov) AS median_aov_threshold,
       CAST(ROUND((SUM(CASE WHEN purchase_amount < median_aov THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) * 100.0) / COUNT(*), 1) AS FLOAT) AS pct_below_median,
       ROUND(SUM(CASE WHEN purchase_amount < median_aov THEN (median_aov - purchase_amount) * 0.25 ELSE 0 END), 2) AS simulated_rev_lift,
       ROUND((SUM(CASE WHEN purchase_amount < median_aov THEN (median_aov - purchase_amount) * 0.25 ELSE 0 END) * 100.0) / SUM(purchase_amount), 1) AS cohort_rev_lift_pct
FROM order_stats;
```

</details>

