## 2. Data Preprocessing & SQL Pipeline

```mermaid
    flowchart LR
        A("customer_shopping_behavior.csv (3,900 rows)") -->|01_data_load_eda.ipynb / pandas| B("Clean, Impute & Feature Engineer")
        B -->|SQLAlchemy + pyodbc| C[("MS SQL Server: da_projects.dbo.customer_behavior")]
        C -->|02_business_analysis.sql| D["Power BI Dashboard (dashboard.pbix)"]
        D -->|Business Rules & RICE Scoring| E["loyalty_and_promo_brd.md"]
```

- **Schema Standardization & Deduplication:**
  - Converted all 18 raw column headers to `snake_case` and renamed `purchase_amount_(usd)` to `purchase_amount`.
  - Verified 100% programmatic equivalence between `discount_applied` and `promo_code_used` and dropped the redundant `promo_code_used` column.
- **Category-Unbiased Null Imputation:** Imputed **37 missing `review_rating` records** using category-partitioned medians (`df.groupby('category')['review_rating'].transform(lambda x: x.fillna(x.median()))`) to prevent cross-category rating distortion.
- **Analytical Feature Engineering & Database Ingestion:**
  - **Demographic Cohorts (`age_group`):** Binned customer ages (`18–70`, median `44`) via `pd.cut` into `'Young Adult'` (`0–25`), `'Adult'` (`26–40`), `'Middle-aged'` (`41–60`), and `'Senior'` (`61–120`).
  - **Numerical Purchase Cycles (`purchase_frequency_days`):** Mapped 7 text frequency strings (`Weekly`: `7`, `Fortnightly` / `Bi-Weekly`: `14`, `Monthly`: `30`, `Quarterly` / `Every 3 Months`: `90`, `Annually`: `365`) into integer day intervals before ingesting the 19-column table into **MS SQL Server** (`da_projects.dbo.customer_behavior`).

