## 4. Product Strategy & RICE Prioritization

To turn these SQL and Power BI insights into an actionable e-commerce roadmap, three candidate growth features were scored using the **RICE Prioritization Framework** (**Reach × Impact × Confidence ÷ Effort**) based on cohort sizes in `dbo.customer_behavior`:

| Initiative                                            | Target Dataset Cohort                      | Reach (Users) | Impact (0.5–3) | Confidence (%) | Effort (Wks) | **RICE Score** | Priority             |
| :---------------------------------------------------- | :----------------------------------------- | :------------ | :------------- | :------------- | :----------- | :------------- | :------------------- |
| **1. Minimum-Spend Promo Gate (`$60+`) & Upsell Bar** | `1,677` Promo Users (`Q2`, `Q6`)           | 1,677         | 2.0            | 90%            | 2.0          | **1,509**      | **P1 — Build First** |
| **2. Repeat-Buyer Checkout Subscription Nudge**       | `2,847` Non-Subscribers (`Q5`, `Q7`, `Q9`) | 2,500         | 1.5            | 80%            | 3.0          | **1,000**      | **P2 — Next Sprint** |
| **3. Automated Cycle Replenishment Triggers**         | `purchase_frequency_days <= 30` (`Q10`)    | 2,181         | 1.0            | 75%            | 3.0          | **545**        | **P3 — Backlog**     |

